implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW (load adversarial-self-review). Read the diff as a hostile child process and as a host that vanishes mid-stream.

Mutation probes: run them in a /tmp `git archive HEAD | tar -x` snapshot with your two files copied in, never in the shared checkout. Confirm each mutant turns a test red:
- raw passthrough of child bytes;
- hello written after spawn;
- an observation built from child data, or written before EOF and waitpid;
- stdin not DEVNULL;
- close_fds=False;
- killpg replaced by kill;
- start_new_session dropped (S6 hangs until its timeout);
- OUTPUT_CHUNK_BYTES raised to 196608 or more;
- the 'SIG%d' fallback removed;
- the euid check removed, or switched to os.getuid (the injected-geteuid case catches it).
For any survivor, either show it is equivalent and give the reason, or add the missing assertion.

Also confirm:
- nothing writes to fd 1 except write_frame (grep for print( and sys.stdout);
- the diff contains no globalRails.forbiddenPatterns entry, in Python and test strings alike. The JS eval-call pattern also matches Python's literal_eval call, and the double-underscore proto key counts too;
- every exception path either returns a documented exit code or kills and reaps the child;
- no __pycache__ exists anywhere under scripts/.
If any byte changed, re-run step 4's command and submit that fresh output as the evidence.
